WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.660
Frieza: " This planet is still going to blow, the core has been completely disintegrated."

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.180
Frieza: "Five minutes!"

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.860
Frieza: "That's how long you have."

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.900
And thus began

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.500
the biggest lie in TV history

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:25.820
[Film Theory Intro Sequence]

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.580
Hello, Internet! Welcome to Film Theory,

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:35.040
where 10 episodes , three hours and thousands of power levels later

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.620
Namek finally exploded

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.820
['In the arms of an angel' plays]

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.280
So, let me come out and say it: Dragon Ball rocks

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.420
[Guitar Riff]

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:50.680
the characters, the villans; but ESPECIALLY the powers

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:55.720
I mean, what self-respecting kid HASN'T pretended to harness their ki and shoot out giant energy balls?

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.320
Or fly around punching faster than speed of light?

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.380
Or stood there screaming for hours 
working to power up?

00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:04.960
Hey, here's a joke for you How many Saiyans 
does it take to screw in a light bulb?

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.760
One! but it'll take three episodes to do it

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.240
[MatPat's singing] Banana Nah

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:11.240
[Still singing] Banananananana

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:18.100
Now, if there's one attack that everyone assosiates with the series, it's Goku's famous "KAMEHAMEHA" WAVE,

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:20.400
or "TURTLE DEVASTATION" WAVE

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.440
Named after the Hawaian king, Kamehameha.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.560
The move is used by everyone, 
from Master Roshi to Buu

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:28.860
And as such, it comes with a bunch of variations.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:30.560
But more often than not,

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:34.820
it consists of the character gathering ki energy between their hands to form an energy ball

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:38.060
that then gets blasted out in a beam towards your big bad

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:41.160
with questionable gender.  #LoveWins

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:44.580
And I have to say, since starting Game Theory four years ago,

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:50.140
I have received SO many emails, tweets, facebook messages from you loyal theorists,

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.880
asking me to look into the physics 
of this attack to figure out

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:56.200
how YOU can start blasting your best friend into your neighbor's backyard.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:57.560
And it was tough!

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.360
I mean, really tough, actually.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:04.460
As what I found forced me to question some of my basic assumptions about how the universe works.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:08.560
And that's no joke, as there were a LOT of revelations during the research for this one.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:13.140
But I THINK we've developed a pretty good theory about what's going on during these moves.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:15.160
So, let's start with what we're given by the show.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:18.040
In the series, all these attacks are based on KI energy,

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:21.100
life force energy that exists inside every living being.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.900
With the major focus being in the center of the body.

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.360
By drawing it out, the user is able to manipulate it, and use it outside the body.

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:33.100
from forming protective KI barriers, to create KI balls and KI blasts to vaporize an opponent.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:38.460
Until inevitably one cell of him manages to survive, and he's able to completely regenerate

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:40.380
even STRONGER than before.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:42.980
Here, have a senzu bean while you're at it.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:44.260
Because THAT makes a lot of sense.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:47.480
Super Saiyan? More like Stupid Saiyan.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:49.080
*whispers* stupid senzu beans...

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.440
Awh, all the world's exsistence hangs in the balance

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:52.780
Mwaa, I want a fair fight

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:57.180
Anyway, I think it'll come as no suprise to anyone to hear that DragonBall's Ki

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.680
is a direct reference to the real life idea of qi... or chi.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:05.260
One of the foundational principals in Chinese medicines and martial arts.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.520
The word literally translates as "Breath", "Air" or "Gas"

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:13.920
and is thought to be a life force, or energy, that exists in everything.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.920
Just like it is in the show.

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:18.580
In Hindu, there is also the concept of chakras

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:21.040
Centers on spiritual power throughout the body.

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:26.900
So chi in real life is a: hard to define, mental/spiritul energy that when mastered can heal the wounded,

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:32.020
stengthen a fighter, even go so far to give them darth vader force like powers!

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:33.700
Similar to what we are seeing in the show

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.200
at least, that's what some people believe.

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.160
but there is one big problem here;

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:42.520
there is no good sources backing any of this up whether you believe in chi energy or not.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:45.940
most of the quote on quote 'Science conducted supporting Chi',

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:49.300
was done by people with a firm belief of holistic medicine.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:52.280
So, defiantly not the most impartial of judges.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:54.580
and neutral researchers well...

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:58.860
They're just not interested in testing videos of people rolling around like idiots.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:06.060
Or, should I say, more importantly, the people with grant dollars aren't interested in funding that sort of research.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:08.320
Which means, no scientists care.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:11.280
So that's a bummer, but of course we're not just gonna leave it at that!

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:15.640
I am not going to let the scientific community's inability to test this stuff

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:18.800
prevent me from shooting energy beams of light out of my hands

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:22.100
I mean, if Krillin can do it, so can I dammit!

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:24.940
and as an aside here, can I just say, how depressing it is

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:29.760
to think that Krillin is one of the strongest human beings alive on that show!

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:31.940
Urgh! that's a sobering thought...

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:34.360
Anyway, we're going to step in where science has failed

00:04:34.360 --> 00:04:38.640
and answer the true question these top research institutions should be looking at:

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:43.400
How does a fictional character shoot a fictional wave of energy out of his hands?

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:47.300
Well, to truly understand what's going on, we have to look at the wave's properties.

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:50.780
and the first thing to note is that this isn't just an energy wave.

00:04:50.840 --> 00:04:55.000
You can't see energy. Energy is a property of a physical thing.

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.980
Something physical has to possess that energy.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:02.460
If you need proof from the show: look at Gohan's Kamehameha wave pushing against Cell's,

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.040
near the end of that story arch.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:08.500
See how his ball of energy causes Cell's to collapse in on itself in response?

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:12.160
It's like if I pushed on a piece of cellophane or Reynolds wrap.

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:17.060
Clearly there's a lot of energy there, but it's being carried in a physical form.

00:05:17.140 --> 00:05:20.060
It is literally a form of matter.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:20.860
What's a 'matter'?

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:22.340
I don't know, what's-a-matter with you?

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:24.040
[needle scratch]
Ha ha...!

00:05:24.040 --> 00:05:24.660
...ooooooh

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:26.340
...Bad Marx jokes aside...

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.300
Matter is anything that takes up space and has mass.

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.760
I'm sure we've all learned the three states of matter right?

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:33.820
Solids, liquids, gases?

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:39.040
Problem is the Kamehameha wave doesn't behave like any of those so... what is it?

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:45.280
Well, I hate to break it to you, but your 3rd grade science teacher has been part of a life long conspiricy...

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:49.380
a cover-up misleading generations of young students!

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:52.220
There aren't just three states of matter...

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:54.520
There's actually a fourth!

00:05:54.680 --> 00:05:55.920
Plasma

00:05:55.920 --> 00:06:01.640
and it's this fourth state of matter that unlocks all the secrets to Dragon ball's energy blasts.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:05.980
In fact, let me tell how big this lie you've been told actually is.

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:11.480
Solids, liquids and gases make up 1% of the universe.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:14.260
One MEASLY percent!

00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:21.840
Matter in a state of plasma makes up the other 99% of the observable universe.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:26.620
Which makes humans, quite literally, part of the 1%

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:29.240
So stop occupying Wall street ya hippies!

00:06:29.240 --> 00:06:33.780
So why have elementary school science teachers hidden this fact from generations of kids?

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:37.700
Well, 3rd grade is pretty early to be learning physical chemistry.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:41.080
Plus, plasma isn't something we run into all that often on Earth.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:44.700
You're probably most familiar with it, thanks to fluorescent light bulbs

00:06:44.700 --> 00:06:46.920
What's lighting up in there? Plasma.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.140
Lightning? Also plasma.

00:06:49.160 --> 00:06:50.600
Stars like our Sun?

00:06:50.600 --> 00:06:53.580
We've all been lead to believe that they're big balls of gas

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:58.000
Even by NASA in an incredibly poorly written definition on their website.

00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.600
Well, that's wrong

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:02.780
They're mostly plasma because of how hot they are.

00:07:02.860 --> 00:07:05.340
And by the way NASA change that please

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:09.040
You can't say it's mostly a ball of gas but then say it's mostly plasma

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:12.060
They are two different states of matter!

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:17.560
It'd be like me saying this turkey sandwich is a ham sandwich just because it has another meat in it.

00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:20.160
They're close, but they're not the same.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.720
Can you tell that I skipped lunch to write this episode?

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:25.580
[MatPat's stomach gurgles]
So before we see how plasma plays a part in Dragonball

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:27.740
we need to know what exactly it is

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:30.740
You know how when you heat up a solid it melts and becomes a liquid

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:32.620
and you heat it up a bit more and it becomes a gas

00:07:32.620 --> 00:07:35.600
Well, if you heat the gas even more it becomes plasma

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:40.760
Basically the electrons in the atoms of the gas get so excited they start to break away.

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:44.820
So what you end up with is this soup of negatively charged electrons

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:50.200
floating along side positively charged ions from the atoms that have lost their electrons.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:54.960
Long-story-short, the main thing to remember is a plasma is a super-heated gas.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:58.440
So when Goku makes a ball of energy appear out of nothing

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.120
that's not 100% true.

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:01.540
There's gas!

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:05.340
Air between his hands that he's super-heating to create that ball.

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:08.880
So the next logical question there is: How is he heating it up?

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:12.600
And the answer is surprisingly simple: Just like a fluorescent bulb.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:16.460
When you turn on a light electricity is sent through the gas in the tube.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:20.180
Super charging the atoms so that the electrons start popping off,

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.980
creating the glowing plasma to illuminate the room.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:26.020
The characters in Dragon ball are doing the same thing.

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:31.160
Their 'Ki power' is really them harnessing their body's electric potential

00:08:31.220 --> 00:08:33.980
and focusing it on area's around them.

00:08:34.040 --> 00:08:34.840
Skeptical?

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:35.960
I hear what you're saying

00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:37.020
but consider this

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:41.600
In the battle against Vegeta, Goku calls upon his triple Kaio-ken attack

00:08:41.680 --> 00:08:43.360
and what do we see happen?

00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:46.700
Electricity starts radiating around his body

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:49.620
His electric potential has sky-rocketed.

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:56.080
And as Super Saiyans ascend to higher and higher levels we see lightening pulsing around their bodies.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:59.480
Lightning, AKA plasma.

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:00.600
but that's not all,

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:04.640
You know how any of these warriors need a huge burst of energy to ascend to the next level

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.060
or start their energy attack?

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:09.960
but then, once they're there, they're able to sustain that power level?

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:13.460
Well, plasma and electric potentials explain that too

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:18.840
To convert any gas to plasma, including air, there's a big start of energy.

00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:21.160
Typically around 33 kilovolts per centimeter

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:28.280
but, once the plasma arch's been created, it can be sustained with only a tenth of that energy

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.820
3 kilovolts per centimeter

00:09:30.820 --> 00:09:34.520
by that same principle the arch needs to be started next to its energy source

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:39.400
but once there, it can be drawn out to ten times the distance from said source

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:43.360
Which, in the case of the Kamehameha wave, is why the wave starts near Goku

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:51.220
and then can A) reach out so far away from him and B) is so much stronger when launched near the opponent

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:56.540
like when Goku choose to fire at point blank at Cell as his last ditch attempt to finish the fight.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:57.400
Speaking of villains,

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:02.840
during the second comeing of Broly we find Kamehameha's can combine to become even stronger

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:08.800
As Gohan, Goten and Goku join forces for the so-called 'Family Kamehameha'.

00:10:08.840 --> 00:10:16.280
It would be a touching moment if I weren't so distracted by the fact that Goku is literally a spirit in this instance!

00:10:16.280 --> 00:10:17.960
If you'll pardon my little rant here,

00:10:17.960 --> 00:10:22.680
but I mean okay, the guy dies and is wished back into existence every 10 episodes.

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:24.540
Fine, I accept that.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:29.280
but for his attack to still be viable when he's still technically a ghost!?

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:30.080
Ugh!

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:36.140
Anyway, the important point here is the separate beams can combine and grow stronger.

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:38.840
Plasma exhibits this same quality.

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:40.540
Look at your typical plasma ball

00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:43.220
No, that's not just an out-dated desk ornament.

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:45.560
It's a lesson on Dragon ball Z physics.

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:48.960
Notice that, as the beam of plasma has a point to focus on,

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:53.040
they combine and grow stronger, bigger and more powerful.

00:10:53.360 --> 00:10:55.540
Just like we see on the show.

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:57.800
And don't worry, I hear your question.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:02.480
If plasma is just superheated gas, how can it obliterate Cell or push people away?

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:05.640
PS: Goku should have won Deathbattle #butthurt

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:08.400
Well listen up, salty Superman hater , because

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:14.180
it's probably the single biggest clue that this beams are plasma instead of just pure energy.

00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:18.640
You see, the wild thing about plasma is that they're nothing like a gas.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:22.440
That why they qualify as a entirely separate state of matter.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:25.800
Remember that this is the stuff than stars are made of.

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:30.240
So Goku is basically creating a small star in between his hands.

00:11:30.420 --> 00:11:34.560
And at high temperature, plasma become thicker, more viscous

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:37.680
to the level that it can physically be pushed.

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:42.640
That's why everyone from Frieza to Buu can try to stop this thing with their hands.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:48.860
It's also how in that earlier example, Gohan's wave is able to push Cell back into the skies.

00:11:48.860 --> 00:11:53.420
It's a denser plasma beam able to overcome the momentum of his attack.

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:56.380
It's also how Goku was able to form a ki shield.

00:11:56.380 --> 00:12:01.980
It's the same plasma shield technology that the company Boeing has just patterned.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:05.600
I kid you not, plasma shield are becoming a real thing.

00:12:05.600 --> 00:12:07.260
Truly, we live in the future.

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:10.540
And you know how characters are always getting into energy clashes

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:13.180
with the two beams struggling for superiority?

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:16.820
Whoever it's Gohan vs Cell or Goku vs Vegeta,

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:19.820
beams colliding is a staple of the show

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:23.660
with that rounded ball shape being iconic of these sorts of stand offs

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:27.140
Would one plasma beam be able to push against another?

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:28.740
Well yes.

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:30.740
In real life, it's difficult to find examples

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:33.200
that are nearly that spectacular or focused

00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:37.460
but putting two plasma balls and watching their beams strikes each other,

00:12:37.720 --> 00:12:40.080
you see them pushing against one another

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:43.380
forcing in to each other up and out until the connection is broken

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:46.120
or they're too far away from their primary energy source.

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:48.600
And then, what about that ball shape?

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:53.300
Well, we can compare the beam collision to that of stars in outer space.

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:58.560
Looking up their collision pattern, with two big balls of plasma combine at moderate to high speeds,

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.560
they splashed outward

00:13:00.560 --> 00:13:02.700
like we see in the Goku/Vegeta battle.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:05.320
But they also fuse together.

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:07.320
Fusion-Ha!

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:09.320
into a swirling mass of energy.

00:13:09.320 --> 00:13:13.700
Their magnetic field reorganize 
into a ball shape before...

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:16.520
well, in space, they create a black hole.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:19.040
In Dragon ball, it doesn't go that far.

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:22.640
Oh sure, the planet will most likely come to a horrific conclusion

00:13:22.640 --> 00:13:26.860
but you know, at least we won't be crushed under the infinite blackness of gravity.

00:13:27.060 --> 00:13:28.100
So, there you have it.

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:32.040
"ki" and "wave attack" are most likely electric potential and plasma.

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:32.900
It's interesting.

00:13:32.900 --> 00:13:37.640
In the end, spiritual energies like Dragon ball's ki or real life chi

00:13:37.640 --> 00:13:42.560
are models created to explain weird trends or natural phenomenon in the world around us.

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:45.900
In that, they're not that far different from a scientific theory.

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:48.980
Theories, by their nature, are incomplete.

00:13:48.980 --> 00:13:50.080
And you know what?

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:52.240
Probably wrong in some ways.

00:13:52.240 --> 00:13:53.900
Sometimes in a lot of ways.

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:57.740
But what they provide is an useful explanation for what we see

00:13:57.740 --> 00:14:02.280
until we inevitably learn more and revise our theories to accommodate that new information.

00:14:02.280 --> 00:14:07.840
In this case, plasma and electric potential work fairly well for a phenomenon we see throughout the series,

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.760
evolve, change, defy it's own logic.

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:13.640
Sorry, just theorizing about theorizing.

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:16.260
I guess I should end on a joke now. Huuum...

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:17.020
Oh I know.

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:19.220
Dragon Ball GT. Bah doum tching.

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:22.960
But heh, that's just a theory.

00:14:23.260 --> 00:14:25.260
A film theory.

